    "['family inet [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ipv4-family unicast', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nipv4-family unicast\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe Juniper command `set protocols bgp group neighbor-172.16.2.2 family inet unicast` enables IPv4 unicast address family for BGP. In HUAWEI devices, the equivalent is achieved by entering the `ipv4-family unicast` sub-mode within the BGP configuration context. \\n\\nNote that in HUAWEI devices, you would typically enter this after configuring the BGP neighbor (peer) settings, similar to how it's structured in Juniper but with different syntax. The complete BGP configuration in HUAWEI would involve multiple commands including the peer AS number configuration before this address family command.\", 'trans_template': 'ipv4-family unicast'}]]": 1,
